nk-800>Fully typed: </strong>Written in TypeScript with complete type definitions and predictable APIs.</li><li><strong class=text-ink-800>Composable: </strong>Higher-level components built from the same primitives you can access directly, so nothing is a black box.'),m7=p(`<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600">SolidJS is one of the most performant and developer-friendly frameworks available today, but its component ecosystem hasn't kept pace. Most UI libraries are built for React and ported over as an afterthought, which means you either deal with impedance mismatches or build everything yourself.`),f7=p(`<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600">TorchUI is built for <!> from the ground up. Every component is a native Solid component, so everything just works the way you'd expect, with no surprising side-effects.`),b7=p(`<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600">For accessible primitives, we chose <!>, the best-in-class headless component library for SolidJS. Kobalte handles focus management, keyboard navigation, and ARIA semantics so that accessibility isn't bolted on after the fact, it's structural.`),v7=p(`<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600">For styling, we chose <!>. Tailwind's utility-first approach pairs well with component-based UIs. Styles live close to the markup, customization is straightforward, and there's no CSS-in-JS overhead. TorchUI's design tokens plug directly into Tailwind's <!> system, so your theme is just CSS variables you own and control.`);const Xd="scroll-mt-24 mt-8",Jd="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-800",Qd="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-600";function y7(){return r(fe,{title:"Introduction",description:"TorchUI is a component library built for SolidJS. It brings together the accessible, unstyled primitives from Kobalte and layers in the styling, layout, and real-world patterns you need to ship consistent, polished interfaces without sacrificing flexibility or accessibility.",get children(){return[r(Ie,{id:"built-on-solid-ground",class:Xd,tit